{number: 78}
{title: Faith of Our Fathers}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[G] Faith of our fathers! [D7] living [G] still,
In spite of dungeon, [C] fire, and [G] sword:
O how our hearts beat [D7] high with [G] joy
Whene’er we hear that [D7] glorious [G] word!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Faith of our [G] fathers, [D7] holy [G] faith!
We [C] will be [G] true to [D7] thee till [G] death.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[G] Faith of our fathers! [D7] we will [G] strive
To win all nations [C] unto [G] thee,
And thro' the truth that [D7] comes from [G] God,
Mankind shall then be [D7] truly [G] free.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[G] Faith of our fathers! [D7] we will [G] love
Both friend and foe in [C] all our [G] strife:
And preach thee too as [D7] love knows [G] how,
By kindly words and [D7] virtuous [G] life.
{end_of_verse}
